# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00203 and Plan 00201 Task 2.18: rebuilds ccy-teams (no CCY or image change). The team
# menu gains "Add a running session to <team>" and every running seat menu gains "Add this
# session to another team" (one flow: pick the session, seat and role); a team not installed or
# with its homeserver down is refused before any question. ccy-teams waits for the play lock (up
# to 30 min, with a visible Stop waiting) instead of failing with exit 75, and never leaves a
# saved-but-unapplied edit. The playwright-tests distrobox cleanup now reports changed only when
# it removes a container. Running sessions are not touched. Plan 00203 Task 2.6: ccy-teams apply
# and lxc-add name the LXC members a play held back because their containers were stopped, lxc-add
# lists the team's declared members in stopped containers before its yes, and the board shows a
# deferred member's row and "container stopped at the last apply" on a joined one.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00203 Task 2.6: a stopped LXC container no longer fails the agent-bus play. A member
# already joined whose container is stopped is skipped (left as it is), one not yet joined is
# deferred and joined by the first run with its container up; each is printed in a task of its
# own. The play writes each team's LXC member record under /var/lib/agent-bus-applied/lxc/,
# which ccy-teams reads. No container is started, and members in running containers are joined
# and refreshed as before.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
